-- title:
--   Sixteen-step Syracuse descent on chunk 3 of the modulus-$2^{26}$ refinement (2400 residue classes)
-- statement:
--   Let $T(n)$ be the odd part of $3n+1$ (the platform's Syracuse map `syracuseStep`), and let $T^{16}$ denote sixteen successive applications. Let $R_3$ be the explicit list of 2400 distinct residues modulo $2^{26}=67108864$ enumerated in the formal statement. For every natural number $n$,
--
--   $$
--   n\bmod 67108864\in R_{3}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad T^{16}(n)<n.
--   $$
--
--   This is chunk 3 of 9 of the modulus-$2^{26}$ refinement of the [twentyseven-branch residual after the modulus-$2^{24}$ refinement](https://prove2.me/theorems/66d0270f-93c1-476d-9046-1def7e102223); the chunks are disjoint and together cover 20423 residue classes, all lying over the leaf's 51280 surviving classes modulo $2^{24}$ and each admitting a descent certificate with exponent budget $26$.
--
--   **Method.** For each $r\in R_3$ the first fifteen Syracuse steps of $r$ are exact rows $3b_j+1=2^{a_j}b_{j+1}$ with $b_0=r$ and odd $b_{j+1}$, with $S=\sum_{j<15}a_j\le 26$, and the sixteenth row is closed by a divisor exponent $e=\min(v_2(3b_{15}+1),\,26-S)$ with quotient $B=(3b_{15}+1)/2^{e}<r$. The published theorem [`CollatzFrontier.syracuse_terminal_budget_of_descent`](https://prove2.me/theorems/2513a4d3-77eb-4b93-9876-33755812122c) then gives $T^{16}(r+2^{26}q)<r+2^{26}q$ for all $q$, and one kernel evaluation of the checker over the literal list closes the chunk.
--
--   **Role.** Together with the other chunks and the refined residual `syracuse_descent_residual_twentyseven_mod32_mod2097152_after_step16_mod67108864` it reduces the open frontier leaf [`syracuse_descent_residual_twentyseven_mod32_mod2097152_after_step15_mod16777216`](https://prove2.me/theorems/66d0270f-93c1-476d-9046-1def7e102223) by a case split on membership in the chunk lists; the chunks together remove $20423/205120\approx 10.0\%$ of the leaf's open classes modulo $2^{26}$ without bounding the starting value or the descent time.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The map is the existing definition `syracuseStep`; the residue list is a literal `List ℕ` inside the theorem's type, as in the earlier list theorems of this branch. The recursion-depth option only supports elaboration of the long literal. No monotonicity of the Syracuse map is asserted.
